From: OpenHarmony PC Developer Community
Subject: [PATCH] boxes 2.3.1 test harness: replace GNU sed extensions with POSIX

The HarmonyOS build worker ships toybox sed, which supports POSIX BRE/ERE only.
Two upstream test files rely on GNU-only escapes that toybox does not implement:

- test/testrunner.sh uses the word-boundary escape \b in the range address
  /^:EXPECTED\b.*$/. toybox reads \b as a literal 'b', so the address never
  matches; the sed range then runs past the :EXPECTED section and copies the
  box border line (/****...) into the generated filter file. Feeding that file
  back through `sed -E -f` aborts with
  "sed: bad regex '****...': Repetition not preceded by valid expression",
  which failed 179 upstream cases. /^:EXPECTED/ is equivalent here (the address
  is already anchored at start-of-line) and is valid POSIX.

- test/173_help_text.txt uses the GNU class \w inside an :OUTPUT-FILTER
  expression; [[:alnum:]_] matches exactly the same characters under POSIX.

Only the harness's own fixture parsing is touched: no test case, assertion or
expected output is altered.

diff -ruN a/test/173_help_text.txt b/test/173_help_text.txt
--- a/test/173_help_text.txt
+++ b/test/173_help_text.txt
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 --help
 :INPUT
 :OUTPUT-FILTER
-s/^(.+?-e, --eol .+?default: )\w+]/\1EOL_DEFAULT]/
+s/^(.+?-e, --eol .+?default: )[[:alnum:]_]+]/\1EOL_DEFAULT]/
 s/^(.+?-f, --config .+?default: ).*/\1GLOBAL_CONFIG]/
 s/^(.+?-n, --encoding .+?default: ).*/\1CHARSET_DEFAULT]/
 :EXPECTED
diff -ruN a/test/testrunner.sh b/test/testrunner.sh
--- a/test/testrunner.sh
+++ b/test/testrunner.sh
@@ -237,7 +237,7 @@
     fi
 
     cat "${opt_testCase}" | sed -n '/^:INPUT/,/^:OUTPUT-FILTER/p;' | sed '1d;$d' | tr -d '\r' > "${testInputFile}"
-    cat "${opt_testCase}" | sed -n '/^:OUTPUT-FILTER/,/^:EXPECTED\b.*$/p;' | sed '1d;$d' | tr -d '\r' > "${testFilterFile}"
+    cat "${opt_testCase}" | sed -n '/^:OUTPUT-FILTER/,/^:EXPECTED/p;' | sed '1d;$d' | tr -d '\r' > "${testFilterFile}"
     cat "${opt_testCase}" | sed -n '/^:EXPECTED/,/^:EOF/p;' | sed '1d;$d' | tr -d '\r' > "${testExpectationFile}"
 }
 
